" gitenv  right identity, right repo                                                             "
"┌ Profiles ──────────────────────┐┌ Current repository ────────────────────────────────────────┐"
"│  ● personal  ada@example.com   ││root        /home/ada/work/acme/api                         │"
"│> ◆ acme  ada@acme.example      ││remote      git@github.com:acme/api.git                     │"
"│    agency  ada@agency.example  ││                                                            │"
"│                                ││Effective identity                                          │"
"│       ┌ Why this profile? ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐       │"
"│       │'acme' claims this repository. Rules that match, strongest first:             │       │"
"│       │                                                                              │       │"
"│       │✔ acme      remote  github.com/acme/*                                         │       │"
"│       │  agency    remote  github.com/**                                             │       │"
"│       │    'github.com/acme/' is more specific than 'github.com/'                    │       │"
"│       │  personal  path    /home/ada/work/**                                         │       │"
"│       │    a remote rule beats a path rule                                           │       │"
